   "text": "For women, cut makes little difference: average front pocket depth is 14.3 for skinny, 14.4 for straight and 14.2 for boot-cut jeans. Paying more does not help either. The correlation between price and front-pocket depth is −0.15 for women's jeans and −0.26 for men's, so pricier jeans, if anything, have slightly shallower pockets."
